T* (- if D1 is 31, set D1 to 30;) Tj T* (- if D2 is 31 and D1 \(after the first rule\) is 30 or 31, set D2 to 30.) Tj T* () Tj T* (The year fraction is days / 360. There is no February end-of-month rule in) Tj T* (the FinTekkers definition \(LM-498\). Some systems, including the spreadsheet) Tj T* (basis 0, add one; results differ when a date is the last day of February.) Tj T* () Tj T* (4 ACT/360 {#act-360}) Tj T* () Tj T* (Actual days over 360. Used for Treasury bills and money-market instruments.) Tj T* (A full year is therefore slightly more than 1.0 \(365/360\).) Tj T* () Tj T* (5 ACT/365 Fixed {#act-365f}) Tj T* () Tj T* (Actual days over 365, in every year, leap years included. Used for some) Tj T* (money-market and sterling instruments and for many curve-building) Tj T* ET
